# Human / production copy

**`ui-minimal-copy.mdc`** decides _whether_ to add text. **This rule** decides _how_ that text must sound.

Any **new** user-facing string (UI labels, helpers, buttons, toasts, empty states, errors, printed documents, reminder messages, AI assistant chat responses) must be short, plain, balanced, and production-grade.

## Hard bans (AI tells)

| Ban | Use instead |
| --- | --- |
| Em dash `—` (U+2014) | Period, comma, colon, or parentheses |
| En dash `–` as a clause break | Hyphen `-` only in compounds |
| Marketing fluff | Plain nouns/verbs: no _seamless_, _robust_, _leverage_, _empower_, _unlock_, _elevate_, _delight_ |
| Tutor voice | No _This lets you…_, _Easily…_, _Simply…_, _Just…_ as padding |
| Fake warmth / hype | No _exciting_, _powerful_, emoji in clinical/billing UI |

## Length bar

| Surface | Target |
| --- | --- |
| Labels / nav | 1-4 words |
| Buttons | 1-3 words (`Save`, `Send`, `Confirm`) |
| Helper / tooltip (only if required) | One short sentence |
| Toast / error | What happened; optional next step |
| AI assistant chat reply | As short as answers the question — never pad with filler before the answer |
| Printed documents (Rx, certificate, receipt) | Match the clinical/legal register — no casual tone at all |

## Before shipping a string

1. Would a careful human writer ship this, or does it read like model default prose?
2. Can it be cut by 30% without losing meaning?
3. Does it contain `—` or fluff words from the ban list?

If unsure, prefer **shorter** or **omit**.
